      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Set up KPI tracking, data protection rules, and dashboard expectations.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 480386,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's finalize our measurement plan. I've drafted a proposal for our core KPIs and the data protection rules. Please see A7 for the data rules and my proposed KPIs for T5 below:\n1. Total Feedback Volume (by channel)\n2. Feedback by Category (% mix)\n3. Average Time to First Response\nThoughts?",
            "mentions": [
              29126,
              17689,
              225681,
              37334
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 225681,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "I've reviewed A7. The data protection rules are clear and align with our standard compliance requirements. Specifically, the rules on anonymizing data for reporting and the 90-day retention period for raw feedback are correct. I'm good with this. This covers T9.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "lock",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 37334,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "The KPIs seem focused on volume and speed. Should we also try to measure the quality or impact of the feedback? For example, tracking the number of 'Actionable Insights' generated per week. It might be subjective, but it would show if the new process is actually useful, not just busy.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 2
